snp1.1:10.2 | S: knowing nothing is what it seems, free of greed. | T: (none)
snp1.1:10.3 | S: Such a mendicant sheds the near shore and the far, | T: (none)
snp1.1:10.4 | S: as a serpent its old worn-out skin. | T: (none)
snp1.1:11.1 | S: They have not run too far nor run back, | T: The monk who hasn’t slipped past or held back,
snp1.1:11.2 | S: knowing nothing is what it seems, free of lust. | T: without greed, as “All this is unreal,”
snp1.1:11.3 | S: Such a mendicant sheds the near shore and the far, | T: sloughs off the near shore & far—
